// src/core/conversation_disk_env.def - every STRATA_* name that appears in src/ and include/, classified for the conversation disk
// tier's key (conversation_disk_tier.cpp builds the key lists from this table; tests/core/conversation_disk_env_test.cpp fails when a
// name in the sources is missing here or a class and the key disagree).  MOD_PLAN 16b "disk-key"; the audit and its evidence are in
// pancake-docs/batch4/disk-key.md.
//
// A NEW switch (any "STRATA_..." string in src/ or include/) needs one line below.  The question to answer: with the same token ids,
// can the switch change a single bit of the state the tier saves (K/V, recurrent state, tails)?
//   yes -> Key or KeyIfSet (KeyIfSet when it was never in the key before, so existing keys of runs without it stay as they were)
//   no, and a test or the docs say the bits are the same, or it only moves work around -> Speed
//   no arithmetic at all (log, trace, path, limit, test hook, another engine) -> Inert
//   cannot tell -> Unsure (keyed when set), and say why in the note
// A name that is only an alias of a fingerprinted setting is InConfig.  Compile-time macros (-DSTRATA_...) are not environment
// variables and cannot be in this key.
//
// STRATA_ENV(name, class, note)



// ---- Key: changes what a conversation state holds; always part of the key (a "-" when unset) (25) ----
STRATA_ENV("STRATA_CPU_PRESUM", Key, "host pre-sums CPU rows (not bit-identical)")
STRATA_ENV("STRATA_EXPDEC", Key, "decode expert kernels family; documented exact, kept in the key conservatively (batch-1)")
